<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills rose to 8.923 percent on Thursday from 8.888 percent at the previous auction on May 28.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt had asked for 1.2 billion pounds and accepted bids for 1,441.375 million, Bills worth 870.450 million pounds mature today.</p>
<p>The Central Bank announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Sept 4, 1997 (Aug 28, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 8.923 percent (8.888)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 1,441.375 million (1,387.025 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,755.500 million (1,647.800 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.399-9.010 percent (8.002-8.998)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.399-10.002 percent (8.002-9.203)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 87 (109)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 106 (140)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1/</p>
</text>
